Subject:	Major 2002 Construction Projects

February 28, 2002

To:	Transcontinental Gas Pipe Line Customers and Shippers

Re:	Major 2002 Construction Projects

The projects listed below are the major pipeline and station 
construction projects that are currently scheduled for the 2002 
construction season.  Dates and duration of these jobs may change prior 
to construction.  Additional information will be forthcoming on a 
particular job if there are significant impacts to available capacity.

Unless specifically stated to the contrary, the following jobs will not 
impact firm transportation.  However, based on past summer operating 
conditions, it is anticipated that interruptible transportation 
services (IT and secondary FT) may be impacted by some of the work.  
The extent of the impact will depend on operating conditions at the 
time of the outages.

Job No. 1 - 
Brazos River, Texas, Smart Pig Project
Smart pig 34 miles of Main Line "B" from the near the Brazos River, 
Texas (M.P. 293.29)(Fort Bend County) to Compressor Station 35 near 
Houston, Texas (M.P. 327.27)(Harris County).  Estimated outage timing 
for preparatory: June 3, 2002, to June 8, 2002.  Estimated timing for 
smart pig runs: June 11, 2002, and June 14, 2002.  Estimated outage 
timing for anomaly repair, if required: September 30, 2002, to November 
8, 2002.

Job No. 2 - 
Brazos River, Texas, Pipe Replacement Project
Replace pipe on Main Lines "A" and "B" between the Brazos River, Texas 
(M.P. 293.29)(Fort Bend County) and Compressor Station 35 near Houston, 
Texas (M.P. 327.27)(Harris County).  Estimated outage timing: June 14, 
2002, to August 6, 2002.

Job No. 3 - 
Amite River, Louisiana, Pipe Replacement Project
Replace pipe on Main Lines "A", "B", and "C" between Compressor Station 
60 near Jackson, Louisiana (M.P. 588.60)(East Feliciana Parish) and 
Compressor Station 65 near Greensburg, Louisiana (M.P. 626.53)(St. 
Helena Parish). During work on Main Line "B", Mid-Louisiana Gas Clinton 
M&R 4399 will be out of service.  Estimated outage timing: August 24, 
2002, to September 26, 2002.

Job No. 4 - 
Momentum Expansion Project
Work on the Momentum Expansion Project will result in brief outages at 
several compressor stations and pipeline segments in September 2002 and 
October 2002.  Outages will occur to tie-in or modify piping at 
Compressor Station 90 near Sweetwater, Alabama (M.P. 811.13) (Marengo 
County); Compressor Station 105 near Rockford, Alabama (M.P. 927.06) 
(Coosa County); and Compressor Station 160 near Reidsville, North 
Carolina (M.P. 1369.40) (Rockingham County).
Job No. 5 - 
Newnan, Georgia, Pipe Replacement Project
Replace pipe on Main Lines "A", "B", "C", and "D" between Compressor 
Station 115 near Newnan, Georgia (M.P. 1007.55) (Coweta County) and 
Compressor Station 120 near Stockbridge, Georgia (M.P. 1048.34) (Henry 
County). Estimated outage timing: April 16, 2002, to July 15, 2002.

Job No. 6 - 
Stockbridge, Georgia, SCC Hydrostatic Test Project
Perform a Stress Corrosion Cracking (SCC) hydrostatic test on 15 miles 
of Main Line "A" between Compressor Station 120 near Stockbridge, 
Georgia (M.P. 1048.34) (Henry County) and Compressor Station 125 near 
