timing: April 6, 2002, to April 30, 2002.

Job No. 7 - 
North Georgia Extension Pipe Replacement Project
Pipe replacement in the last two valve sections (Gwinnett County) at 
the end of North Georgia Extension Lateral 16-inch line; lateral 
originates at Compressor Station 125 near Monroe, Georgia (M.P. 
1085.97) (Walton County). During work in the valve section at the far 
end of the lateral, the City of Lawrenceville Lawrenceville M&R 7013, 
the Atlanta Gas Light Suwanee M&R 7203, the City of Buford West Buford 
M&R 7197, and the City of Sugar Hill M&R 7217 will be out of service.  
Estimated timing for the outage at end of lateral with meter stations 
out of service: June 13, 2002, to June 15, 2002.  Estimated outage 
timing for the other valve section with meter stations remaining in 
service: June 21, 2002, to July 22, 2002.

Job No. 8 - 
Comer, Georgia, Smart Pig Project
Smart pig 81 miles of Main Line "B" from Compressor Station 130 near 
Comer, Georgia (M.P. 1124.71)(Madison County) to Compressor Station 140 
near Moore, South Carolina (M.P. 1205.80) (Spartanburg County).  
Estimated outage timing for preparatory: June 8, 2002, to June 15, 
2002.  Estimated timing for smart pig runs: June 18, 2002, and June 20, 
2002.  Estimated outage timing for anomaly repair, if required: June 
22, 2002, to October 1, 2002.

Job No. 9 - 
Grover, North Carolina, Pipe Replacement Project
Replace pipe on Main Lines "A", "B", "C", and "D" between Compressor 
Station 140 near Moore, South Carolina (M.P. 1205.80)(Spatanburg 
County) and Compressor Station 145 near Grover, North Carolina (M.P. 
1247.03)(Cleveland County).  Estimated outage timing: April 20, 2002, 
to May 27, 2002.

Job No. 10 - 
Sundance Expansion Project
Work on the Sundance Expansion Project will result an outages at 
Compressor Station 150 near Mooresville, North Carolina (M.P. 
1287.11)(Iredell County) from March 8, 2002, to March 10, 2002

Job No. 11 - 
Mooresville, North Carolina, Pipe Replacement Project
