Yesterday SoCal filed the attached Advice Letter No. 2837-A to implement re=
vised operating procedures under Rule 30 of their tariff.  Basically this w=
ill formalize the October announcement to discontinue the Windowing process=
 calculations effective November 1, 2001.  Instead SoCal will utilize the M=
aximum Operating Capacity at each receipt point as the capacity limit.  Lyn=
n attended the referenced October meeting and subsequently distributed the =
handouts which are also part of the attachment, however if anyone needs add=
itional copies of  them please let me know. SoCal views this filing as an i=
nterim step towards approval of the GIR/Unbundling proceeding which will pr=
ovide for a system of firm tradable intrastate transmission rights.  I'll c=
ontinue to monitor the proceeding and will advise of any further actions ta=
ken by SoCal or their customers.  gh

